1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:10,217
A Wood Mackenzie analysis reported by gCaptain says the record expansion of global LNG supply could be slowed by shipbuilding limits.

2
00:00:10,167 --> 00:00:18,255
Most LNG carriers are built in a small group of Asian yards, while demand for new ships is rising.

3
00:00:18,255 --> 00:00:28,991
The bottleneck matters for energy markets because gas projects need vessels before they can reliably serve Europe, Asia, and other importers.

